<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Scattered showers seen over Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Scattered showers seen over Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Friday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		   16.0</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    17.9</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   7.0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 18.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     12.8</p>
<p>    Norton		   21.5</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   4.2</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department said scattered showers accompanied by thunder at times will be experienced in the Western, Central, Sabaragamuwa and Southern provinces on Friday. There will also be fairely strong winds over the western slopes of the central hills, the department said.</p>
</text>
